From 0ce673cf3d56607abfdfe32e8dd883622755f92d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johnjose <jjose@carboncopies.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:37:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional Neurotransmitter argument to the pair strength
 routes (LIFC)

Simulation/SetPrePostStrength, BatchSetPrePostStrength (string for all
entries or one per pair) and SetAllStrength accept an optional
"Neurotransmitter" ("AMPA" | "GABA" | "NMDA"). When given, only the receptor
group of that type between the pair is set (weight = conductance / summed
peak conductance of that group); groups of other types are not touched, and a
failed request (no group of that type, negative conductance, invalid type)
changes nothing. When absent the behavior is exactly the previous one (first
AMPA group set, all other groups from that presynaptic neuron zeroed).

- LIFCNeuron::UpdatePrePostStrength(pre, G, NT = -1)
- Simulation::UpdatePrePostStrength / UpdateAllStrength / UpdateBatchPrePostStrength take NT
- BallAndStick/SC neurons reject the argument
- unit tests in SimulationReceptorStrength.test.cpp (new; Simulation.test.cpp
  is currently not compiled by CMake)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
